Claude Usage Plasmoid
=====================

A panel widget for KDE Plasma 6 that shows your Claude Code usage limits
-- the 5-hour session window and the 7-day rolling window -- read
directly from Anthropic's OAuth usage API.  It is the Plasma equivalent
of the Waybar widgets claudebar and ai-usagebar.

The compact form shown in the panel is a dual ring: the 5-hour window on
the outside, the 7-day window on the inside, with the higher of the two
percentages in the centre and coloured from green to red as usage rises.
Clicking it opens a popup with labelled progress bars, a countdown to
each reset and the extra-credit balance.  A middle click forces a
refresh.


How it works
------------

`contents/scripts/fetch-usage.sh' reads the OAuth token that the
`claude' CLI writes to `~/.claude/.credentials.json' and queries

    https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage

caching the result for 55 seconds.  The QML front end
(`contents/ui/main.qml') polls that script once a minute through a
Plasma5Support DataSource and renders the result with Kirigami.  The
token is only ever sent to Anthropic; nothing is written anywhere but
the local cache.


Requirements
------------

Plasma 6 (Qt 6 / Kirigami) at run time, plus `curl', `jq' and `bash'
for the fetch script.


Installation
------------

Run

    ./install.sh

which symlinks the package into
`~/.local/share/plasma/plasmoids/io.github.gpontespc.claudeusage' so that edits are
picked up live.  Then right-click the panel, choose "Add Widgets" and
add "Claude Usage".

To try it in isolation, without touching your panel, run

    plasmoidviewer -a io.github.gpontespc.claudeusage

from the plasma-sdk package.


Notes
-----

The widget does not refresh the OAuth token itself; it relies on the
`claude' CLI keeping `~/.claude/.credentials.json' current.  When the
token has expired the widget reports it and asks you to run the `claude'
CLI to renew.

Only Anthropic is supported.  The fetch script is small and is the only
place that would need changing to add another vendor.
